<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred von Tirpitz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred von Tirpitz was a German admiral and State Secretary of the Imperial Naval Office from 1897 to 1916. He directed the build-up of the German High Seas Fleet under the naval laws, intended to challenge British naval supremacy. The resulting naval arms race worsened Anglo-German relations before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and was a central part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>'s military policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-von-tirpitz.jpg" alt="Alfred von Tirpitz" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_134-C1743,_Alfred_von_Tirpitz_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
